> git tag -f <tag-name>


Forcing Tags

> Git will yell at us if we try to reuse a tag that is already referring
  to a commit. If we use the -f option, we can FORCE our tag though.

> git tag
> git log --oneline
> git tag v18.6.1 6986e68767be
fatal: tag 'v18.6.1' already exist
> git tag v18.6.1 6986e68767be -f
Updated tag 'v18.6.1' (was 142545dt2234)